<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Deliberately empty for the Developer ID channel.

	  Hardened Runtime is a signing option (the runtime flag on codesign), not an
	  entitlement. It does not restrict the child processes Forma starts: the
	  DEVONthink MCP helper is a separate, signed executable launched through
	  Process(), so no library-validation escape hatch is needed.

	  No App Sandbox (com.apple.security.app-sandbox). If an App Store channel is
	  ever chosen, sandbox plus security-scoped bookmarks are a separate,
	  unverified workstream (docs/MACOS-VALIDATION-BACKLOG.md M8).

	  No com.apple.security.automation.apple-events: Forma must not reach
	  DEVONthink through AppleScript.

	  No full-disk access: the only directories Forma reads are the ones the user
	  grants through a panel, stored as security-scoped bookmarks.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
